    {
      "id": "solve-in-place",
      "name": "solveInPlace",
      "category": "TriangularMatrix",
      "signature": "solveInPlace(Other)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Other",
          "type": "MatrixBase<OtherDerived>&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<OtherDerived> EIGEN_DEVICE_FUNC void",
      "docs": "\"in-place\" version of TriangularView::solve() where the result is written in \\a other\n\\warning The parameter is only marked 'const' to make the C++ compiler accept a temporary expression here.\nThis function will const_cast it, so constness isn't honored here.\nNote that the template parameter \\c Side can be omitted, in which case \\c Side==OnTheLeft\nSee TriangularView:solve() for the details."
